;; Sequence-occurrence route tripwire (docs/sequences.md §5.3 discharge
;; note; 2026-09-06 audit).  The seq-index x DRed^c story is discharged by
;; ROUTE EXCLUSION: $seq_at/$seq_atr carry no counted capability (the
;; daemon's `$` filter), so every certificate over a seq-probing cone must
;; fail and a retraction must take clear-and-rerun.  That exclusion rests
;; on three implicit facts -- this fixture is the tripwire if any of them
;; is refactored away (a maintain route over this cone would run flavored
;; artifacts that carry NO SeqIndexTask, silently under-deriving).
;;
;; `want` anchors a head-position probe (hitn); `kw` anchors an independent
;; end-position probe (kwhit) so a partial cone leaves $seq_at protected as
;; a shared side channel -- its stale rows must stay harmless.

table (want int)
table (kw int)
table (doc (list int))
table (hitn int)
table (kwhit int)

rule (doc [7 1 2]) (doc [3 7 9]) (doc [1 2 3])
rule (kw 9)

rule
(want v)
(doc l)
(= l [v xs ...])
-->
(hitn v)

rule
(kw v)
(doc l)
(= l [xs ... v])
-->
(kwhit v)
